flowchart TD
    accTitle: Multi-agent topologies and failure amplification
    accDescr: An intermediate-level flowchart comparing coordinator, pipeline, and peer-mesh topologies. A potentially flawed claim or plan branches through the three topologies, then reaches a check before reuse. Detection leads to containment or revision, while an absent or unsuccessful check allows the error to spread into the final output.

    A["Potentially flawed claim or plan enters the system"] --> B{"Interaction topology"}

    B --> C["Coordinator topology"]
    C --> C1["One coordinator distributes a plan"]
    C1 --> C2["A shared mistake reaches multiple workers"]

    B --> P["Pipeline topology"]
    P --> P1["Agents act in sequence"]
    P1 --> P2["An early mistake changes the state used downstream"]

    B --> M["Peer-mesh topology"]
    M --> M1["Peers exchange messages"]
    M1 --> M2["A mistake is repeated across peer messages"]

    C2 --> G{"Check before another agent reuses it?"}
    P2 --> G
    M2 --> G

    G -- "Yes" --> H["Compare with evidence or an independent review"]
    H --> I{"Issue detected?"}
    I -- "Yes" --> J["Correct, isolate, or stop the affected path"]
    J --> K["Contained or revised result"]

    I -- "No" --> L["Residual error continues"]
    G -- "No" --> L
    L --> N["Amplification risk: agents copy, transform, or reinforce the error"]
    N --> O["Final output carries the error"]
